1
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,600
THIS SHOW IS CREATED
FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:06,360
THE CHARACTERS, BEHAVIORS
AND EVENTS ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:08,840
THEY ARE NOT INTENDED TO DEFAME
OR CAUSE DAMAGE

4
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:10,920
TO ANY ORGANIZATION OR INDIVIDUAL
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED

5
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:26,920
Seehan never trusts anyone easily.
Especially enemies.

6
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,800
You have to trick him
into believing you really killed me.

7
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:33,800
How did my parents die?

8
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,120
I killed them.

9
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:38,080
I killed them myself.

10
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:48,280
<i>I worked with Paisan and Decha.</i>

11
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,920
They're now dead.

12
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,080
Someone has to take responsibility.

13
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:15,880
I haven't shot a gun in ages.

14
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:18,520
Wonder if I've lost my touch.

15
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:25,680
People like you ruin this country.

16
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,400
It's just business.

17
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,920
Whoever has more money buys more power.

18
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,840
And then you sell out the country

19
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:44,240
so scumbags like you can profit.

20
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:48,440
No. You're wrong.

21
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:52,280
I just make a profit
from a world that's already like this.

22
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,480
Stop being so naive.

23
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:04,560
You assholes are no better
than mangy dogs.

24
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:11,240
I'm doing you a favor.

25
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:15,120
Maybe you won't be
so stupid in your next life.

26
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,560
In my next life,

27
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,680
I'll be a vet.

28
00:04:19,839 --> 00:04:23,960
Because even a mangy dog is
more loyal than politicians like you.

29
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,720
Ugh.

30
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:40,960
I received a report of
an illegal detention of a civilian here.

31
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:46,560
What game are you playing?

32
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,080
We had a deal.

33
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:52,560
Or did you change your mind?

34
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,000
It was a setup.

35
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,040
You're trying to arrest me?

36
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,720
I definitely will if I have evidence.

37
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,240
And do you?

38
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:17,560
<i>What are you going to do with me?</i>

39
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:22,280
<i>Going to court is a waste of time.</i>
<i>I'll pass judgment myself.</i>

40
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,440
Don't be mad at me, man.

41
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:29,800
I can't survive on my own
in this corrupt system.

42
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,720
Gun once told me something, too.

43
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:40,200
In a shady world like this,
you've got to be shady too.

44
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,560
Don't claim that's AI.

45
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,760
You planned this with him?

46
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
I'm just doing my duty
as a police officer.

47
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,240
Take her away.

48
00:05:58,280 --> 00:05:59,280
Hey.

49
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,120
Back off.

50
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:04,240
Duty? You'll soon learn

51
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:07,640
that righteousness can't buy shit.

52
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,960
Whoever puts a bullet in their heads,

53
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:18,480
I'll pay a million per bullet.

54
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,840
-Hey, get down!
-What the hell?

55
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,080
I said get down!

56
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,600
Down!

57
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:27,760
Ouch!

58
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:32,520
-You bastards are cops!
-Kill them all.

59
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,200
-Go, go, go!
-Come on!

60
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:49,800
Go!

61
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,640
Take them out.

62
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:01,440
Ma'am, take cover.

63
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,480
-Stay here.
-Yeah.

64
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,760
Stop.

65
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,080
I surrender.

66
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,320
I surrender.

67
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,120
Wait, wait.

68
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:14,040
Think you're so tough?

69
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,160
Screw this!

70
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,320
Gosh.

71
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:26,000
Damn it.

72
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:28,640
Damn you.

73
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,400
Had enough, ma'am?

74
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:44,840
Hey.

75
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,440
Aren't you a cop?

76
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,600
They kill people too.

77
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:01,880
Why only arrest me? Why not arrest them?

78
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:07,200
I remember, during your speeches,

79
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:11,040
you always addressed
the "honorable guests."

80
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,160
So today,

81
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,120
I'll give you the honor.

82
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,080
Come here.

83
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:22,560
Resisting arrest makes it worse for you.

84
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:24,800
You'll see who you messed with.

85
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,440
You dare arrest me?

86
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:34,040
Aut, take her away.

87
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:36,440
Come on.

88
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,640
I can walk on my own.

89
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,640
After you, then.

90
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,080
Gun.

91
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:55,480
Thank you so much.

92
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:57,960
Thank you too,

93
00:10:58,640 --> 00:10:59,680
for playing along.

94
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,320
Hold on.

95
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:07,240
What did you two plan?

96
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:11,800
Gun sent me the location so I could
arrest you as part of Sirin's plan.

97
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,520
And neither of you

98
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:19,720
said a word to me?
I thought I was really being sold out.

99
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,960
Well, your acting was too realistic.

100
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,760
Next time, you two tell me first.
I almost fricking died.

101
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,280
You guys aren't leaving?

102
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,440
You do your duty.

103
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:40,600
I'll do mine.

104
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:47,880
Not leaving? Then I am.

105
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:28,960
What's the plan now?

106
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:34,000
We have to get to him
before he flees the country.

107
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:39,080
After what happened today,
he'll definitely be planning his escape.

108
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:44,840
I can help.

109
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:47,720
I know where he'll go.

110
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:54,040
<i>If he wants to run,</i>

111
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:56,000
<i>he'll need to retrieve his hidden cash</i>

112
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,640
<i>to set up a new base abroad.</i>

113
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,640
I won't let this chance slip away.

114
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,080
What do you have in mind?

115
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,000
This time,

116
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:17,960
I want to choose my own path.

117
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:35,560
-Stay still.
-You think just because you caught me,

118
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:37,400
I'll go to jail without a fight?

119
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,800
-Huh?
-Stay still.

120
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:42,960
Jail is for the poor and the stupid.

121
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,240
That's true.

122
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,640
I think jail doesn't suit you.

123
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:56,320
People like you belong in hell.

124
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:57,640
Hey.

125
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:00,080
Don't get smart with me.

126
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:03,680
I have connections
with prosecutors, with judges.

127
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:05,000
No one can touch me.

128
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:09,240
Let's not waste our breath.

129
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:13,560
Save your words for the courtroom.

130
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:15,520
Let's go.

131
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:19,600
The moment I make bail,
you'll be the first to die.

132
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:23,600
Then I'll have to make the case

133
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:25,360
against you airtight before you get out.

134
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,640
Hurry up and get her out.

135
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:42,200
You're going to help her, sir?

136
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:43,760
Help her?

137
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:46,800
I'm helping myself. Hurry up and go!

138
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:47,720
Yes, sir.

139
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,360
Thun.

140
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:51,680
Silence her.

141
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,800
Ma'am!

142
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:55,200
Pack it up faster.
What are you dawdling for?

143
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,320
Boss. No one can trace
anything back to you now.

144
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:08,920
Good.

145
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,880
At least you never fail a job.

146
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:16,480
Hurry up and move the money.
Then go keep watch out front.

147
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,600
Hey.

148
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:26,200
Don't let a single baht
of my money go missing.

149
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:31,880
Get going.

150
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,600
At least I can trust you, Thun.

151
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:43,520
Hey, faster!

152
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:52,960
You're really digging your own graves.

153
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,280
<i>Thun.</i>

154
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,720
Gun and his friend
are on the second floor.

155
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:03,040
Go deal with them right now.

156
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:05,120
Hurry up to the second floor. Go!

157
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,360
Go!

158
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:13,760
He's seen us.

159
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:18,520
Which means they're waiting for us now.

160
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:43,240
Methee, I'm going to make a scene.

161
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:44,960
<i>Pinpoint Seehan's location.</i>

162
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,920
You got it. Consider it done.

163
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:18,800
Boss, I'll handle him myself.

164
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:22,400
What can you do to him? Stay here with me!

165
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:25,320
Hey, you guys go down
and bring his corpse up!

166
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:31,120
What are you standing around for?
Pack the money!

167
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:39,400
Target spotted. Engaging.

168
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:58,480
Target missed. Target still active.

169
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:03,400
Why the hell are you hiding? He's shooting
from across the way. Go get him!

170
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:07,240
And if you fail, don't ever
let me see your face again.

171
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:08,800
-Go!
-Yes, sir.

172
00:20:15,080 --> 00:20:16,240
Come out.

173
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:29,840
Damn it.

174
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:39,840
We have to do it.

175
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:18,120
Gun. Rada. You okay?

176
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:20,280
Gun! Rada!

177
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:31,360
You go find Seehan.
I'll handle things here.

178
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:59,040
You want to play it like this, huh?

179
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:02,680
Yeah.

180
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:06,480
I'm not sniping.
I'm taking you down right here.

181
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:09,600
You ungrateful bitch.

182
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:12,200
You're trying to stand in my way?

183
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:14,880
Not standing in your way.
I'm here to kill you.

184
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:37,880
Hey, stop!

185
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:41,720
Put the gun down.

186
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:44,480
Now!

187
00:24:57,960 --> 00:24:59,440
This world is weird.

188
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:02,640
The people I used,

189
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:05,880
the people I raised,

190
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:10,320
have ended up ganging up on me
and pointing guns at me.

191
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:13,240
Hilarious.

192
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:24,520
It's not hilarious.

193
00:25:25,520 --> 00:25:28,000
Karma just walks a little slower than you.

194
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:30,280
Do you really believe

195
00:25:30,840 --> 00:25:35,200
there's anything money can't buy?
Are you willing to bet on that?

196
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:39,920
I don't know

197
00:25:41,360 --> 00:25:43,720
if righteousness can win.

198
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:49,000
I just know people like you
shouldn't be above the law anymore.

199
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:53,720
You always listen to your heart
instead of your head.

200
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:02,040
You too, you little bitch.

201
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:07,400
I took you in, gave you a new life,

202
00:26:08,760 --> 00:26:10,600
and in the end, you chose him.

203
00:26:14,360 --> 00:26:15,600
People who truly love you

204
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:20,440
don't use loyalty to trap you like this.

205
00:26:23,560 --> 00:26:25,440
Love doesn't exist in this world.

206
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:29,360
Only idiots

207
00:26:31,040 --> 00:26:34,800
would be manipulated by the word "family."

208
00:27:05,640 --> 00:27:08,800
Seehan, let Rada go!

209
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:12,880
Shoot me. I dare you.

210
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:16,720
You're going to get
the one you love killed.

211
00:27:16,800 --> 00:27:17,720
Take this!

212
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:18,840
Rada!

213
00:27:23,960 --> 00:27:25,040
You…

214
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:26,920
Do it.

215
00:27:27,520 --> 00:27:28,440
Shoot him!

216
00:27:29,080 --> 00:27:32,200
Shoot me! Hurry. She told you to shoot.

217
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:34,880
Shoot me. You've been hunting me
for a long time, haven't you?

218
00:27:38,600 --> 00:27:39,760
Shoot!

219
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:44,400
No. I won't trade you for him.

220
00:27:45,400 --> 00:27:46,760
Someone like him.

221
00:27:47,360 --> 00:27:52,240
If he lives,
he'll just destroy other people's lives.

222
00:27:54,600 --> 00:27:57,760
Don't have the guts to do it?
Then shoot me.

223
00:28:04,120 --> 00:28:06,920
Come on. Come and shoot me.

224
00:28:08,280 --> 00:28:11,360
In the end, you got your lover killed.

225
00:28:15,520 --> 00:28:16,400
You…

226
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:23,120
You called the cops to help?

227
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:25,840
You were right about one thing.

228
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:28,960
Not everyone in the system is good.

229
00:28:30,440 --> 00:28:34,560
But some won't sell themselves
for your money.

230
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:36,280
And you think the law can stop me?

231
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:39,800
Huh? They all take my money.

232
00:28:43,120 --> 00:28:44,840
It was corrupt before.

233
00:28:53,120 --> 00:28:56,640
Because scumbags like you
used money to trample it into the dirt.

234
00:28:58,520 --> 00:29:01,480
You think you can change anything, cop?

235
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:09,680
At least today, law enforcement
isn't on your side anymore.

236
00:29:11,280 --> 00:29:13,360
You said the system is broken, didn't you?

237
00:29:14,400 --> 00:29:15,680
You're just afraid

238
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:19,760
that one day, the system
won't stand by you anymore.

239
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:22,880
You will never catch me.

240
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:29,400
Rada! Bastard! I told you to let her go!

241
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:42,560
Rada!

242
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:45,880
Hey!

243
00:30:06,720 --> 00:30:08,000
Why did you ask to meet me?

244
00:30:08,760 --> 00:30:10,720
Chill out. You just got here.

245
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:13,880
I've been hunting them for years.

246
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:20,120
I think the only way to stop him
is to kill him.

247
00:30:21,880 --> 00:30:25,480
I think so too. Shooting him
would end it once and for all.

248
00:30:26,520 --> 00:30:27,920
But someone will take his place.

249
00:30:30,320 --> 00:30:31,840
I've killed so many people.

250
00:30:33,240 --> 00:30:37,160
I can barely tell the difference
between me and him anymore.

251
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:40,200
What do you want me to do?

252
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:43,440
I'll buy as much time
as possible. As for you,

253
00:30:44,200 --> 00:30:45,400
do your duty.

254
00:30:46,320 --> 00:30:48,280
What if he won't go quietly?

255
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:51,200
Then let the law pull the trigger.

256
00:30:52,720 --> 00:30:56,760
If he's going to die, I want him to die
because of what he built.

257
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,040
Not because of my bullet.

258
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:03,520
You trust me that much?

259
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:07,160
I've never believed in the system.

260
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:09,800
But I believe in you.

261
00:31:12,160 --> 00:31:14,480
The scariest thing isn't bad people.

262
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:19,040
It's when good people lose hope
and stop fighting.

263
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:22,160
If that time comes

264
00:31:23,600 --> 00:31:25,680
and I'm still solving
problems with bullets,

265
00:31:26,880 --> 00:31:28,680
nothing will ever change.

266
00:31:52,640 --> 00:31:54,240
Rada. Rada.

267
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:02,600
Careful, Methee.

268
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:13,080
Rada. Hey.

269
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:16,800
Hey. Can you hear me?

270
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:27,360
It's over, right?

271
00:32:30,040 --> 00:32:31,040
Yes.

272
00:32:32,240 --> 00:32:33,320
It's over.

273
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:41,080
Hey…

274
00:32:43,400 --> 00:32:46,400
Don't forget your promise.

275
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:50,680
I…

276
00:32:53,160 --> 00:32:55,520
I want to go live with you.

277
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:01,000
I won't.

278
00:33:04,320 --> 00:33:06,120
I won't forget the promise.

279
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:24,000
Rada.

280
00:33:28,360 --> 00:33:32,000
Rada. Wait. Rada, stay with me.

281
00:33:33,560 --> 00:33:36,800
Rada, listen to me. Rada.

282
00:33:38,560 --> 00:33:40,000
Stay with me, Rada.

283
00:33:40,720 --> 00:33:44,360
Wake up, Rada. Rada. Rada!

284
00:33:45,600 --> 00:33:47,600
Rada, stay with me! Rada!

285
00:33:53,040 --> 00:33:54,080
Rada.

286
00:33:57,920 --> 00:34:00,720
Rada, stay with me. Stay with me.

287
00:34:01,800 --> 00:34:02,800
Rada.

288
00:34:08,120 --> 00:34:10,719
Rada!

289
00:34:14,400 --> 00:34:16,159
Rada!

290
00:35:09,560 --> 00:35:10,640
Holy shit.

291
00:35:12,840 --> 00:35:13,800
What took you so long?

292
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:30,360
Why do you keep following me?
Just let me go.

293
00:35:31,120 --> 00:35:32,760
I can't let you go.

294
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:35,920
Here.

295
00:35:37,240 --> 00:35:41,280
Then put the handcuffs on me,
so you can finally lock me up.

296
00:35:43,480 --> 00:35:47,240
With skills like yours, it might be
better if you worked with me.

297
00:35:52,520 --> 00:35:54,600
I've got warrants out for my arrest, man.

298
00:35:55,920 --> 00:36:00,600
Every problem has a solution.
It just depends on who signs the paper.

299
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:05,600
A guy like you breaking the law?

300
00:36:05,680 --> 00:36:08,240
Well, who was it that said it?

301
00:36:08,320 --> 00:36:10,000
In a shady world,

302
00:36:10,080 --> 00:36:11,320
you've got to be shady too.

303
00:36:12,240 --> 00:36:13,520
Right?

304
00:37:17,560 --> 00:37:19,040
You brought it with you?

305
00:37:19,840 --> 00:37:21,480
Well, its owner is right here.

306
00:37:35,360 --> 00:37:38,960
I never thought we'd ever see this day.

307
00:37:42,680 --> 00:37:46,520
From now on, we won't have
to run from anyone ever again.

308
00:37:52,960 --> 00:37:56,240
Thank you for making my dream come true.

309
00:38:07,160 --> 00:38:08,360
Our dream.

310
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:58,800
THE END

311
00:39:23,760 --> 00:39:26,640
-Pretty crowded over there, huh?
-<i>Nine, eight…</i>

312
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:28,760
<i>Action!</i>

313
00:39:42,640 --> 00:39:45,040
-Alright, awesome, awesome!
-Nice.

314
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:48,480
They're blocked.

315
00:39:48,560 --> 00:39:49,920
-What?
-Are your ears blocked?

316
00:39:50,640 --> 00:39:52,040
Did you shoot it?

317
00:39:52,120 --> 00:39:54,840
-Only one shot?
-Come on. It's easy.

318
00:39:55,680 --> 00:39:57,200
-Action!
-Go, go!

319
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:04,840
Cue exit.

320
00:40:18,720 --> 00:40:21,920
<i>Cut! Leads, come down now.</i>

321
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:24,880
-Come over here, come here.
-Come take cover first.

322
00:40:24,960 --> 00:40:27,040
Come on. Keep walking.

323
00:40:28,360 --> 00:40:31,920
Once he said "action," Esther bolted.

324
00:40:32,920 --> 00:40:34,480
Okay.

325
00:40:34,560 --> 00:40:35,640
Did I go too fast?

326
00:40:35,720 --> 00:40:36,880
Esther moved so fast.

327
00:40:39,080 --> 00:40:43,280
He barely finished "action,"
and she was already gone!

328
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:45,680
She has to be ready.

329
00:40:45,760 --> 00:40:48,720
-I was scared, so I bolted.
-Right, bombs and guns everywhere.

330
00:40:48,800 --> 00:40:49,800
So scary.

331
00:41:28,160 --> 00:41:32,680
Subtitle translation by: Anan Pratchayakul
